Subject: [PATCH] lubot: chain: cagrisiz tavan akisi kaldirildi - taban 327'den 325'e

Ceilings negotiation (CeilingsReport, ceilings_request, parse_ceilings) was the half of
tools::chain the module header never promised - the header says this module reads
outcomes and converts them to corpus lines - and the tree carries no caller for it:
measured with the gate's own reference scan, and with a grep of every file type, the only
mentions outside chain.rs were inside gates/check.py's prose. Delete-biased policy from
the audit loop says an unowned surface leaves rather than gathers documentation; the
allow-list lost bud_aiGetCeilings with it, so the method set again equals the parsers
that exist, and the surface test now asserts the removal in both directions: every
allowed method parses, and a method with no parser is refused.

Baseline consequence, proven by the gate and not asserted: with the two entries gone,
the same scan that reported 53 unreached names now reports 51, and the stale-entry rule
forces the baseline file to shrink in the same patch - first live trip of that direction
on real deletions rather than a synthetic canary. README test count follows to 325.

Not compiled: no Rust toolchain in this sandbox (measured unreachable); brace balance,
gate pass (39/39 rc=0 on the edited tree), and test-name grep are the verification
floor, labeled as such per series policy.
